    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0076" n="72" xml:id="pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/12316: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-05T19:00:00+09:00">February 5, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 5—8:27 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. My unnumbered January 31, 5 p.m. via Shanghai.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d84-f1"/>
                    We were told at the Foreign Office that the Minister for Foreign Affairs,
                    replying to a request for clarification of his statement in the Diet of January
                    25 that “both internally and externally the present struggle is in fact a war”,
                    stated at a meeting this afternoon of the Budget Committee of the Lower House
                    that: Japan has not claimed the rights of a belligerent and this position was
                    not in any way changed by the Government’s statement of January 16<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d84-f2"/> (see our 32, January 16, 3 p.m.).</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for relay to Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
